    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can I trade on Earn2Trade?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Futures only, on the four CME Group exchanges: CME, COMEX, NYMEX, and CBOT. No stocks, no options, no spot forex, no crypto, no CFDs. Pure futures shop."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What futures contracts can I trade?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Equity index (ES, NQ, YM, RTY plus micros MES/MNQ/MYM/M2K), energy (CL, NG plus MCL), metals (GC, SI plus MGC), rates (ZB, ZN, ZF, ZT), currencies (6E, 6B, 6J plus M6E/M6B), agricultural (ZC, ZS, ZW), softs, and Bitcoin micros (MBT subject to current allowance). The full CME/CBOT/NYMEX/COMEX product slate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are micros allowed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - and micros get a favorable progression-ladder treatment (10 micros = 1 contract for ladder purposes). MES, MNQ, MYM, M2K, MGC, MCL, M6E, MHG, M6B all qualify. Micros are how new traders survive the EOD drawdown while learning sizing."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade options on futures?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Options on futures are not supported on Earn2Trade evaluations or funded accounts. Only outright futures contracts."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade spreads?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Outright legs only. Calendar spreads or inter-product spreads as exchange-defined products are generally not supported on retail prop infrastructure. Confirm with Earn2Trade support if you have a specific spread strategy."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are Earn2Trade's trading hours?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "CME hours: Sunday 5:00 PM CT through Friday 4:00 PM CT, with daily 60-minute maintenance breaks. Earn2Trade evaluation accounts force a 3:50 PM CT daily flatten - all positions closed by then."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When must I close positions on the evaluation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "3:50 PM CT every trading day. No overnight holds during TCP or Gauntlet Mini evaluation. Auto-flatten kicks in at 3:50 if you haven't closed manually."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade on US holidays?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Whenever the underlying CME exchange is open - Earn2Trade follows CME's calendar. Some holidays have early closes; some products close earlier than others (cattle futures close earlier than ES). Plan around the exchange's session schedule."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is news trading allowed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - Earn2Trade has no news-trading restriction. Trade FOMC, NFP, CPI, ECB, all of it. This is friendlier than Topstep (which restricts max position into news) and similar to Apex."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is scalping allowed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - discretionary scalping is permitted. The lines are: no HFT/sub-second algorithmic execution, no spoofing, no platform exploits. Standard manual scalping with 10s-30s holds is fine."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does each Earn2Trade plan cost monthly?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "TCP25 / GAU25: ~$90/month (often closer to $75 with 50% promo discounts). TCP50 / GAU50: ~$70/month. TCP100 / GAU100: ~$200-$250/month. GAU150: ~$300/month. GAU200: ~$350/month. Earlier $50/month TCP25 pricing has lapsed. Pricing changes with promotional cycles - check Earn2Trade's purchase page for current rates."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are there free resets?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - one free reset is included every time your monthly subscription is rebilled. As long as you stay subscribed, you get one fresh restart per billing cycle. Big advantage versus Apex's pay-per-reset model."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the cost of a paid reset?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Effective May 1, 2025: TCP25/TCP50/GAU50 reset prices are dynamic with promotions (kept below new-subscription cost). Larger accounts have fixed pricing - TCP100: $00. GAU100: $00. GAU150: $30. GAU200: $55. Paid resets are extra (above the included free monthly reset)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's Earn2Trade's refund policy?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No refunds. Earn2Trade calls their products \"irrevocable\" - once paid, you don't get money back, including on automated subscription renewals. Cancel before the next billing date to avoid being charged."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I cancel my subscription?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Cancel via your Earn2Trade dashboard before the next billing date. Once canceled, you lose access to evaluation accounts, simulator, and educational material immediately - and Earn2Trade cannot reinstate the same evaluation due to technical reasons. So plan accordingly."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is the activation fee still $39?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - $39 one-time for non-professional CME status LiveSim. As of 2025 it's no longer charged upfront - deducted from your first profit withdrawal only. If you don't withdraw profits, you don't pay it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are there discount codes available?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - Earn2Trade runs frequent promo codes (often 30%, 50%, or 60% off first months). Codes change monthly and around seasonal events. Check coupon aggregators or Earn2Trade's email list before purchasing."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is the discount only for the first month or recurring?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most promo codes apply to the first 1-2 months only. Some longer-term codes exist (e.g. INBOX60X12 has been spotted as 12-month 60% off in past cycles), but those are rarer. Standard pricing kicks in after the promo period."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are subscription fees tax-deductible?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For US traders treating prop trading as a business, subscription fees, reset fees, activation fees, education courses, and trading software (PickMyTrade, journaling tools, VPS) generally qualify as Schedule C business expenses. Consult a CPA for your specific situation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are reset fees refundable?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Once a reset is purchased and applied, it's not refundable. Same irrevocable-purchase policy as the main subscription."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which countries can join Earn2Trade?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most countries globally are eligible. Restricted countries (due to OFAC sanctions, KYC/AML constraints, or data-feed provider rules) include: Afghanistan, Albania, Azerbaijan, Burma (Myanmar), Central African Republic, Cuba, Gibraltar, Iran, Iraq, Kenya, Libya, Mali, Nauru, Nigeria, North Korea, Pakistan, Russia, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Syria, Turkmenistan, Ukraine, Venezuela, and Yemen. Palestine is also unsupported by the data feed provider. The list shifts with policy changes - verify your country on the purchase page before subscribing."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need to be a US citizen to get funded?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No - Earn2Trade has historically been one of the better futures props for non-US traders. Non-US citizens submit a W-8BEN (with FTIN) instead of a W-9. Routing may be through Appius (UK partner) instead of Helios depending on geography."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are there US states/territories restricted from payouts?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - Rise (Earn2Trade's primary US payout method) doesn't support certain US locations due to state-level regulations. Check the help center's \"Payout Update for Traders in Certain U.S. States and Territories\" article for the current list before purchasing."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the W-8BEN form?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "IRS form for non-US individuals certifying foreign tax status. Required before your first payout if you're outside the US. Includes your country of residence and, where applicable, an FTIN (Foreign Tax Identifying Number). Whether an FTIN is required is country- and treaty-dependent - not universal. Determines withholding rates under any applicable tax treaty."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the FTIN?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Foreign Tax Identifying Number - your home country's equivalent of an SSN/EIN. Required on the W-8BEN. India's PAN, UK's UTR, EU national tax IDs, etc. all qualify."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What if my country is added to the sanctions list mid-evaluation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If your country is newly sanctioned during your evaluation, you can't continue or reset. Purchases or resets from newly-sanctioned countries are not refunded - Earn2Trade holds a no-refund policy on this scenario too."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the minimum age to trade with Earn2Trade?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "18 years old. Standard for retail prop firms."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Earn2Trade send tax forms to international traders?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Generally no - non-US traders don't get a 1099. You're responsible for reporting prop trading income in your country of residence. The W-8BEN you submitted establishes your non-US tax status with the prop firm; your domestic tax filing is on you."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are payouts to crypto wallets supported internationally?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - direct crypto withdrawals are one of the two documented payout channels (Rise being the other), with a small network/processing fee. Useful for international traders in countries where Rise's local bank rails have weaker infrastructure."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I change my country of residence on my account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, but it triggers KYC re-verification - and can change your routing partner (Helios vs Appius) and your payout method. Contact Earn2Trade support to initiate the country change rather than trying to do it through the dashboard alone."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Earn2Trade vs Topstep - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Topstep is better for traders who want the largest community and a polished proprietary platform (TopstepX). Earn2Trade is better for traders who want a defined scaling path to $400K, the friendlier EOD drawdown, news trading allowance, and education-bundled subscriptions. Topstep's profit split (90/10 for new traders) edges Earn2Trade's 80/20."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Earn2Trade vs Apex Trader Funding - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Apex wins on profit split (90% vs 80%), one-time eval fees vs monthly, no consistency rule on evaluation, and explicit automation friendliness (EAs allowed). Earn2Trade wins on built-in scaling to $400K with no new evaluations needed, free monthly resets, included education, and EOD drawdown across every account type (Apex offers EOD only on certain account variants). Anecdotal community data suggests Apex has a higher first-attempt pass rate, but Earn2Trade does not publish official pass-rate figures."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Earn2Trade vs MyFundedFutures (MFFU) - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "MFFU has multiple plan tiers, friendlier to automation, faster first payout (5 winning days), and 100% retention on first $0K. Earn2Trade wins on built-in scaling, education depth, and decade-long track record. Both have similar evaluation difficulty."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Earn2Trade vs Tradeify - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tradeify is newer (2023) but rapidly grown - known for Tradeify Elite Live (real-money trading after $80K cumulative payouts). Earn2Trade is the older, more established option with a longer track record. Both support PickMyTrade connections via Tradovate and Rithmic. Always check Earn2Trade's official website for their current compliance guidelines on automation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why is Earn2Trade's profit split lower than competitors?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Trade-offs: Earn2Trade gives you free monthly resets (Apex charges per reset), education bundled in (Apex doesn't include curriculum), built-in scaling to $400K with no new evaluations (Apex caps at $300K and requires fresh evals to grow), and a longer-running, well-known brand. The 80/20 split is the price for those features."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which futures prop firm has the easiest evaluation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Hard to rank precisely because most firms don't publish audited pass rates. Community-reported figures suggest Apex has the highest first-attempt pass rate, with MFFU and Tradeify roughly comparable. Earn2Trade does not publish a pass-rate statistic, but the 30% consistency rule plus the 10-day minimum tend to make the evaluation feel stricter than competitors. Pass rate alone isn't the full picture - payout reliability and post-funding rules matter more long term."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which futures prop firm pays out fastest?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "MFFU and Apex tend to be quickest on first payout. Earn2Trade's weekly Wednesday cycle is consistent, but the friction is the Friday 2PM CT cutoff plus the activation-fee deduction on first payout. After first payout, Earn2Trade is roughly comparable to peers."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why do some traders prefer Earn2Trade over flashier newer firms?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Decade-long track record (most prop firms launched in 2020-2024). Survived the 2024-2025 prop firm collapse wave. Affiliated funded operator (Helios) under shared ownership for nearly as long. Real education bundle. The TCP scaling structure is genuinely unique. Customer support is consistently praised on Trustpilot. For \"boring reliability,\" Earn2Trade is a known quantity."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Earn2Trade good for beginners?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - the bundled education, structured Bootcamp option, friendlier EOD drawdown, and free monthly resets make it more beginner-friendly than Apex (which assumes you already know how to trade). The evaluation is still strict thanks to the 30% consistency rule, but at least you have a curriculum to lean on."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Earn2Trade good for advanced traders?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For advanced traders who value scaling without re-evaluation: yes. PickMyTrade supports Tradovate and Rithmic connections for Earn2Trade accounts. Always check Earn2Trade's official website for their current compliance guidelines before deploying automation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why did my evaluation account fail unexpectedly?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most common reasons: hit the daily loss limit, busted the EOD drawdown floor at end-of-day close, exceeded the Progression Ladder contract count (account blocked for the day, not failed but feels the same), or held a position past 3:50 PM CT. The dashboard shows the specific trigger."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "My account got \"blocked\" instead of failed - what's the difference?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "\"Blocked\" usually means a Progression Ladder violation - your account is locked for the rest of the trading day but automatically unlocks at next market close. You don't need to reset. \"Failed\" means a hard rule breach (drawdown bust, daily loss hit) - you'd need to reset to continue."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why does my Earn2Trade dashboard show different P&L than NinjaTrader?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Earn2Trade's dashboard updates may lag the platform during heavy load. Most differences trace to commissions, exchange fees, or the dashboard not yet processing your most recent fills. If the gap is sustained or larger than commissions can explain, contact support with timestamps and screenshots."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "My Rithmic data feed disconnected - what do I do?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Reconnect via your trading platform's connection panel. If repeated, check Rithmic's status page for outages. If outage-related losses occurred, document timestamps/screenshots and email support - Earn2Trade reviews outage cases individually."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "I passed but didn't receive my funding offer - what now?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Funding offers come from Helios or Appius (depending on geography), not directly from Earn2Trade. Email checks: spam folder, \"Helios Trader Group\" or \"Appius Trading\" sender names. If 5+ business days have passed without contact, message Earn2Trade support to escalate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "My first withdrawal got denied - why?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most common: didn't have $239+ in profit ($00 minimum + $39 activation fee), KYC mismatch (name/address inconsistency), W-9 or W-8BEN not submitted, or your country's payout method wasn't yet provisioned. Resolve each item with support and re-request."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why is my LiveSim performance different from Live?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "LiveSim uses a simulated execution engine against live data. Real Live accounts route to the CME - slippage, queue position, partial fills can differ. The most-reported gap is small but consistent ($X cheaper or more expensive average fills). For most retail-size trading, the difference is sub-$50 per session."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "I held past 3:50 PM CT by accident - am I done?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The auto-flatten will close the position at 3:50. The closure itself is a rule reminder rather than an automatic fail. If the auto-flatten fill was poor enough to bust drawdown or daily loss, that bust is what fails the account - not the late hold itself. Plan around the 3:50 cutoff to avoid surprises."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "My consistency rule violation triggered at the worst time - am I doomed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Not doomed. The rule doesn't fail you - it just blocks the pass until you trade more. Calculate: highest day's profit ÷ 0.30 = total profit needed. Keep trading conservatively to add to the total without breaking other rules."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I contact Earn2Trade support?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "In-dashboard chat is the fastest. Email support is also available via the help center. Trustpilot reviews consistently mention quick response times - specific support agents (Ikbal, Ayush, Ysmarlin) are mentioned by name in many reviews."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What if Earn2Trade closes my account for prohibited conduct?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Severity-based: warnings for first-time accidental issues, account resets for moderate violations, permanent closures for pattern violations or willful manipulation. No refunds on closure. Appeal via support with documentation if you believe the decision was incorrect."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why is my Tradovate connection failing for my Earn2Trade account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most common: wrong username (Earn2Trade-issued Tradovate login differs from a personal Tradovate account), expired credentials after subscription lapse, or Tradovate maintenance windows. Verify in your Earn2Trade dashboard that Tradovate is the platform you selected, then re-authenticate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I set trading time restrictions in PickMyTrade for my Earn2Trade account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PickMyTrade includes a Trading Time feature available across all supported broker connections. You can configure specific active trading windows with start and end times (24-hour ET format). Any TradingView alerts received outside your configured hours are automatically rejected — no new trades are placed. Existing open positions remain active. Settings can be applied to specific accounts or all accounts at once. Full guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/trading-time-settings/ For Tradovate accounts, PickMyTrade also integrates with ForexFactory to automatically pause trading before and after scheduled news events — it can close open positions and cancel pending limit/stop orders during news windows. Tradovate Trading Time guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.trade/docs/trading-time-settings/"
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
